<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afgooye</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Afgoi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Afgooye is a town on the Shabelle river in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, about 30 kilometres north-west of Mogadishu. From the early 18th century it was the seat of the Geledi clan and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobroon-dynasty">Gobroon dynasty</a>, who ruled the Sultanate of the Geledi in the fertile lower Shabelle valley. The town is known for its annual Istunka festival of mock stick fights.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afgooye.jpg" alt="Afgooye" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Guillain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afgoye,_Somalia.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
